Subject: libgit2: finish the SecureTransport handshake after checking the server

libgit2 asks SecureTransport to break out of the handshake at server
authentication, checks the certificate, then returns without calling
SSLHandshake again, leaving SSLWrite to finish it. Mac OS X 10.9's
SecureTransport does not: SSLWrite returns errSecBadReq (-909, "Bad parameter
or invalid state for operation"), so cargo fetched no HTTPS git dependency on
10.9. Calling SSLHandshake until it completes, as Apple documents for
kSSLSessionOptionBreakOnServerAuth, works on every macOS.

--- a/vendor/libgit2-sys-0.18.7+1.9.6/libgit2/src/libgit2/streams/stransport.c
+++ b/vendor/libgit2-sys-0.18.7+1.9.6/libgit2/src/libgit2/streams/stransport.c
@@ -120,6 +120,13 @@
 		return GIT_ECERTIFICATE;
 	}
 
+	do {
+		ret = SSLHandshake(st->ctx);
+	} while (ret == errSSLWouldBlock);
+
+	if (ret != noErr)
+		return st->error != 0 ? -1 : stransport_error(ret);
+
 	return 0;
 
 on_error:
